+# VIBEBOX - macOS Sandbox for Agents
+
+## What is VIBEBOX?
+
+VIBEBOX is a per-project micro-VM sandbox for running coding agents on macOS using Apple's Virtualization Framework. It provides a **Debian Linux VM** with fast warm-up times (<5s), explicit mount allowlists, and reusable sessions.
+
+**Key Benefits:**
+- ✅ **Real isolation**: Linux guest VM with hard boundary from host
+- ✅ **Fast re-entry**: <5s warm-up time after first run
+- ✅ **Project-scoped**: Explicit mounts, repo-contained changes
+- ✅ **Safe by default**: Host system sealed off from VM
+
+## When to Use VIBEBOX
+
+Use VIBEBOX when you need to:
+- Execute **untrusted or dangerous commands** safely
+- Test **destructive operations** without risking host files
+- Run **build processes** that might modify the system
+- Isolate **network operations** or external tool execution
+- Test **agent workflows** in a controlled environment
+
+## How to Start VIBEBOX
+
+### Starting the VM
+
+From any project directory:
+
+```bash
+cd /path/to/project
+vibebox
+```
+
+**What happens:**
+1. First run: Downloads and provisions Debian base image (~1-2 minutes)
+2. Subsequent runs: <5s warm-up using cached image
+3. Creates `vibebox.toml` and `.vibebox/` directory automatically
+4. Drops you into shell: `vibecoder@vibebox:~/<project>$`
+
+### Keeping VIBEBOX Running
+
+**Important:** VIBEBOX has an **auto-shutdown timer** (default: 20 seconds of inactivity).
+
+To keep it running for extended testing:
+- Run `vibebox` in a separate terminal
+- Keep the terminal open
+- The VM stays running as long as the session is active
+
+To exit: Type `:exit` inside the VIBEBOX shell
+
+## VIBEBOX Environment
+
+### VM Specifications
+
+- **OS**: Debian GNU/Linux with kernel 6.12.63+
+- **Architecture**: ARM64 (Apple Silicon)
+- **Resources**: 2 CPU cores, 2GB RAM, 5GB disk
+- **Auto-shutdown**: 20 seconds (configurable in `vibebox.toml`)
+
+### Available Tools
+
+- ✅ **Git**: `/usr/bin/git`
+- ✅ **Python**: `/usr/bin/python3` (Python 3.13.5)
+- ✅ **Build tools**: gcc, make, cmake
+- ✅ **Network tools**: curl, wget, ssh
+- ❌ **Node.js**: Not installed by default
+- ❌ **Bun**: Not installed by default
+
+### Project Mounting
+
+Your project is mounted at **`~/<project-name>`** inside the VM:
+- Host: `/Volumes/SanDisk1gb/OhMyFloyd`
+- Guest: `/home/vibecoder/OhMyFloyd`
+
+**Security features:**
+- `.git` directory is **masked** (tmpfs mount) - prevents accidental git operations
+- `.vibebox` directory is **masked** (tmpfs mount)
+- All other files are accessible read-write
+
+## Using VIBEBOX from Agents
+
+### SSH Access Pattern
+
+To execute commands inside VIBEBOX from agents:
+
+```bash
+# SSH into the running VM
+ssh -i /path/to/project/.vibebox/ssh_key \
+    -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no \
+    -o UserKnownHostsFile=/dev/null \
+    vibecoder@<VM_IP> "<command>"
+```
+
+**Example:**
+```bash
+# Get VM IP from instance config
+VM_IP=$(grep vm_ipv4 /path/to/project/.vibebox/instance.toml | cut -d'"' -f2)
+
+# Execute command inside VM
+ssh -i /path/to/project/.vibebox/ssh_key \
+    -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no \
+    -o UserKnownHostsFile=/dev/null \
+    vibecoder@$VM_IP "cd ~/project-name && ls -la"
+```
+
+### Finding VM IP Address
+
+The VM IP is stored in `.vibebox/instance.toml`:
+
+```bash
+# Get current VM IP
+grep vm_ipv4 .vibebox/instance.toml
+# Output: vm_ipv4 = "192.168.64.7"
+```
+
+### Common Operations
+
+**Execute single command:**
+```bash
+ssh -i .vibebox/ssh_key -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no \
+    vibecoder@192.168.64.7 "python3 --version"
+```
+
+**Execute multiple commands:**
+```bash
+ssh -i .vibebox/ssh_key -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no \
+    vibecoder@192.168.64.7 "cd ~/project && pwd && ls -la"
+```
+
+**Copy files from VM to host:**
+```bash
+scp -i .vibebox/ssh_key -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no \
+    vibecoder@192.168.64.7:/tmp/result.txt ./
+```
+
+**Copy files from host to VM:**
+```bash
+scp -i .vibebox/ssh_key -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no \
+    local-file.txt vibecoder@192.168.64.7:/tmp/
+```
+
+## VIBEBOX CLI Commands
+
+```bash
+vibebox              # Start or attach to current project VM
+vibebox list         # List all known project sessions
+vibebox explain      # Show mounts and network info
+vibebox reset        # Delete .vibebox and recreate on next run
+vibebox purge-cache  # Delete global cache (~/.cache/vibebox)
+```
+
+## Configuration (vibebox.toml)
+
+The `vibebox.toml` file is auto-created in your project root:
+
+```toml
+[box]
+cpu_count = 2
+ram_mb = 2048
+disk_gb = 5
+mounts = [
+    "~/.codex:~/.codex:read-write",
+    "~/.claude:~/.claude:read-write",
+]
+
+[supervisor]
+auto_shutdown_ms = 20000  # Auto-shutdown after 20s inactivity
+```
+
+**Customization:**
+- Adjust `cpu_count`, `ram_mb`, `disk_gb` for performance
+- Add extra mounts in `mounts` array
+- Increase `auto_shutdown_ms` for longer sessions
+- Run `vibebox reset` after changing `disk_gb`
+
+## Important Notes
+
+### Security Model
+
+- **Hard VM boundary**: Linux guest is isolated from macOS host
+- **Explicit mounts**: Only specified directories are accessible
+- **Repo-first**: Project files mounted by default, everything else opt-in
+- **Masked directories**: `.git` and `.vibebox` are read-only tmpfs
+
+### Limitations
+
+- **No Node.js/Bun**: Install inside VM if needed: `curl -fsSL https://bun.sh/install | bash`
+- **Git operations**: `.git` is masked - use git from host instead
+- **Auto-shutdown**: VM shuts down after 20s of inactivity (configurable)
+- **Apple Silicon only**: Requires Apple Silicon Mac (M1/M2/M3/M4)
+
+### Performance
+
+- **First run**: ~1-2 minutes (downloads Debian base image)
+- **Subsequent runs**: <5s warm-up (uses cached image)
+- **Disk usage**: 5GB per project instance
+- **Network**: NAT mode with SSH port 22
+
+## Troubleshooting
+
+### SSH Connection Timeout
+
+**Problem**: `ssh: connect to host <IP> port 22: Operation timed out`
+
+**Solution**: VM may have shut down. Restart VIBEBOX:
+```bash
+vibebox  # This will start/attach to the VM
+```
+
+### VM IP Changed
+
+**Problem**: Old VM IP no longer works
+
+**Solution**: Get new IP from instance config:
+```bash
+grep vm_ipv4 .vibebox/instance.toml
+```
+
+### Permission Denied
+
+**Problem**: `Permission denied (publickey)`
+
+**Solution**: Ensure you're using the correct SSH key:
+```bash
+ssh -i .vibebox/ssh_key vibecoder@<VM_IP>
+```
+
+### Disk Full
+
+**Problem**: VM disk is full
+
+**Solution**: Increase disk size in `vibebox.toml` and reset:
+```bash
+# Edit vibebox.toml: disk_gb = 10
+vibebox reset  # Recreates VM with new disk size
+```
+
+### Need to Install Tools
+
+**Problem**: Required tool (Node.js, Bun, etc.) not available
+
+**Solution**: Install inside VM:
+```bash
+# Install Node.js
+curl -fsSL https://deb.nodesource.com/setup_lts.x | bash -
+apt-get install -y nodejs
+
+# Install Bun
+curl -fsSL https://bun.sh/install | bash
+```
+
+## Best Practices
+
+1. **Keep VIBEBOX running** in separate terminal for extended work
+2. **Use for testing** destructive operations before running on host
+3. **Install tools** inside VM once and reuse across sessions
+4. **Monitor disk space** - VM has limited 5GB by default
+5. **Use host for git** operations - `.git` is masked inside VM
+6. **Leverage Python** - pre-installed and ready to use
+7. **Test agent workflows** in isolation before host execution
+
+## Example Workflows
+
+### Safe Command Execution
+
+```bash
+# Test dangerous command in VIBEBOX first
+ssh -i .vibebox/ssh_key vibecoder@192.168.64.7 \
+    "cd ~/project && rm -rf test-dir"
+```
+
+### Python Development
+
+```bash
+# Run Python script in isolated environment
+ssh -i .vibebox/ssh_key vibecoder@192.168.64.7 \
+    "cd ~/project && python3 script.py"
+```
+
+### Build Testing
+
+```bash
+# Test build process in VM
+ssh -i .vibebox/ssh_key vibecoder@192.168.64.7 \
+    "cd ~/project && make clean && make"
+```
+
+### File Operations
+
+```bash
+# Copy test results from VM to host
+scp -i .vibebox/ssh_key vibecoder@192.168.64.7:/tmp/results.txt ./
+```
+
+## Summary
+
+VIBEBOX provides a **fast, isolated Debian VM** for safe agent operations on macOS. Start with `vibebox`, execute commands via SSH, and exit with `:exit`. Perfect for testing, development, and running untrusted code safely.
+
+**Remember**: Keep VIBEBOX running in a separate terminal to avoid auto-shutdown during extended work!
